From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:03:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): let agents pick the account for a child
 session

Belongs with the subscription-accounts series (carried on custom while the
design is discussed on upstream issue #503; see docs/providers.md). Drop it
once upstream has an equivalent.

A session could choose its provider at creation, but a child an agent
started with sys_session_create always shared its parent's runner, and so
its accounts. A Claude session on Databricks could not start one child on a
Claude subscription and another on a Codex subscription.

sys_session_create takes an optional provider, the name of a providers:
entry on the parent's host:

- The runner checks it against the host's config before anything is
  created: an unknown name or a subscription that is not signed in fails
  with the configured names or the sign-in command.
- A provider the parent's runner already uses for its CLI families keeps
  the child co-located. Any other gets the child its own runner on the
  parent's host and workspace, created with provider_override, so the host
  validates and launches it like any session on that provider. The server
  no longer inherits the parent's runner for such a child, and never moves
  it back onto an ancestor's runner when its own is not connected yet.
- Once the server resolves the child's harness, a provider that cannot run
  it deletes the child and lists the providers that can. The first message
  is posted only after that check, so no turn starts on the wrong account.
- provider works with agent_id only; config_path refuses it.

sys_list_models reports host_providers: each provider's name, kind, label,
the CLIs it serves, the CLIs that use it by default from this runner, and
whether it is signed in.

A child in its own runner does not wake its parent when it finishes (the
inbox is runner-local); the tool result and docs say to check it with
sys_session_get_info. Its runner acknowledges the completion instead of
making the forwarder retry for minutes.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit f72a7ba03eae839f9dff878bfa34669902c32daf)
